  "result": "Excellent! All 109 tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've added tier-based automatic discounts to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/customers.js`**: \n   - Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant with discount percentages by tier:\n     - gold: 5%\n     - silver: 2.5%\n     - standard: 0%\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`**:\n   - Imported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` from customers.js\n   - Updated `createInvoice()` to apply tier discount when a line doesn't have its own `discountPercent`\n   - Updated `addLine()` similarly to apply tier discounts to new lines\n   - Logic: A line's explicit `discountPercent` (including 0) always overrides the tier discount\n\n3. **Tests**: \n   - Updated 4 existing tests to account for tier discounts (changed customer to standard tier where needed)\n   - Added 12 new tests covering:\n     - Tier discounts applied correctly for each tier (gold, silver, standard)\n     - Line discount overrides tier discount (including 0 override)\n     - Multiple lines with mixed explicit and tier discounts\n     - `addLine()` applies tier discounts\n     - `invoiceTotals()` correctly calculates discounts with tiers\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- Lines without explicit `discountPercent` get their customer's tier discount\n- Lines with explicit `discountPercent` (even 0) always use that value\n- Standard tier customers (0% discount) don't get a `discountPercent` field on lines\n- Gold tier gets 5% automatic discount, silver tier gets 2.5%",
